            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did veṟṟilai mean, and what did varavēṟpu mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ஆகாயம்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஆகாயம் (ākāyam) — \"the sky\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit ākāśa, the open lit space. Malayalam and Telugu both keep the ś their letters can write and say ākāśaṁ. Tamil has no letter for that sound, so the word arrives softened, with a ய standing where the ś was, and settles as ஆகாயம் (ākāyam)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tamil's own inherited word for the same overhead space is vāṉ, which you have already met inside vāṉilai, the weather — the standing of the sky. ஆகாயம் (ākāyam) took the wider and emptier sense: not the weather over your head but the space itself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five things above you."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "ākāyam",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *ākāyam*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "vaṇakkam, then ākāyam, as you would greet somebody out of doors",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *vaṇakkam*, then *ākāyam*, as you would greet somebody out of doors]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
