        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: சூரியன்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சூரியன் (sūriyaṉ) — \"the sun\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit sūrya, and the three sisters differ only in what they hang on the end of it. Telugu makes సూర్యుడు (sūryuḍu), Malayalam sūryan, Tamil சூரியன் (sūriyaṉ). The ending is the part each language owns; the sun is shared."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tamil's inherited sun is ñāyiṟu, the word standing behind the name of the first day of the week you already count through. It stepped back into the calendar and into poetry and left the daily sun to சூரியன் (sūriyaṉ)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: the space, and the thing that lights it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
