          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மேகம் (mēkam) — \"a cloud\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit megha, taken in whole. Tamil has inherited cloud-words too — mukil and kār, both still alive in names and in verse — but மேகம் (mēkam) is the one doing the daily work."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Telugu did not borrow here at all: its cloud is mabbu, its own. Which words a language takes and which it keeps is rarely tidy. On the sky the two of them borrowed together; on the cloud they part."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is the whole sky: the space, the sun, the moon, the small lights, and the thing that hides them."
            }
          ]
        },
